a devastating fire it happened in  downtown las vegas over the weekend  leaves many looking for a new place to  live and city leaders are letting them  know we are here for you several  buildings and some two dozen cars were  destroyed in that fire near fremont and  eastern sally jaramillo joins us now  live from there with the efforts to help  those find a new place to live sally  brian and denise the red cross along  with councilwoman olivia diaz want the  community to know that they're only one  phone call away fire crews were out here  earlier looking for clues on who or what  could have started this  we know that you know it's going to be a  while before we recover and we can  rebuild councilwoman olivia diaz is  devastated by the fire but relieved no  lives were lost the city along with the  red cross are making sure everyone  affected gets help so we haven't seen  nearly as many residents as we would  have assumed that we would have so  that's why we're really encouraging  those who haven't checked in with us to  just  make that phone call marcus laner who  has lived at the freeman urban town home  lobs for almost three years is grateful  for the assistance my wife and i and a  friend of ours we were out at a bar  having a good time and uh our neighbor  had called us and let us know that the  neighborhood was on fire i had to like  stop like what he's like the  neighborhood's on fire and i had my dogs  inside the house and he has a key to my  house so i immediately was like bro if  it's safe for you to do it go to my  house and just grab my dogs that's all i  care about right now laner says his  truck was destroyed in the fire  it's heartbreaking it really is  a lot of these people lost a lot and i  hope that they're getting the help that  they need and as we get ready to  celebrate the fourth of july diaz  message i just really really would like  all of our families to make sure that  their fire alarms are up to date that  the batteries are installed properly  that if they're older than 10 years  they're switched out be smart about  fireworks this year and just be safe you  know keep your family safe  back out live tim samanski with las  vegas fire and rescue tells me they will  be back here tomorrow morning with an  arson dog to further investigate all of  this for now reporting live from  downtown sally caramillo live local now
 

